[Music]  there were warnings before this day of  rallies that president jaya bolsonaro  was undermining brazilian democracy  he's trailing the former president luis  inacio lula de silva in opinion polls  for next year's elections which he says  he's not prepared to lose  we don't want disruption we don't want  to fight with any branch but we can't  accept anybody's efforts to distort our  democracy we can't accept anybody who  puts our freedom at risk  he's referring to the supreme court  which is investigating him and members  of his family on corruption charges his  handling of the pandemic has also cost  him support almost 600 brazilian deaths  have been recorded  but i do fear the impact of the actions  of bolsonaro towards the quality of  brazilian democracy because we have seen  in the last years bolsonaro undermining  the strength of many democratic  institutions  such as the national congress the  judicial power  his attacks on the free press and so on  president bolsonaro however still enjoys  substantial support and he called on his  loyal followers to show it  a president elected with 57 million  votes can't be accused of organizing a  coup that's a lie because he won the  presidency in the first round  what we want is freedom of expression to  be able to work  we want a free brazil in which the  people are heard bolsonaro lets us speak  many of his opponents stayed at home  saying they wanted to prevent clashes  but they believe the tide is turning  against the president who divides brazil  it's not just political groups here but  a protest of people who are here to  defend democracy the other protest is by  those defending a coup attempt  bolton has a strategy of destruction he  is violent a terrorist since he was  young and unfortunately he's now arming  the population  tight security kept the rival rallies  apart and there were few violent  incidents reported however they clearly  showed that brazil is as polarized now  as it has been for many years and both  sides are preparing for what threatens  to be a long and bitter election  campaign  daniel schweinler al jazeera

